  "dedup": "No near-identical alternatives or discarded scenario fields. Each client source is complete. Common algorithms live in separate implementation pairs and official proposed LMX core.",
  "comparability_decisions": [
    "uniq Perl uses string equality/undef; integer usage is a common domain; generic unique(same) implementation comparison is separate.",
    "splice client converts end-exclusive bound to Perl length visibly; changed target and removed values are both returned.",
    "split empty string gives one empty field by shared contract; Perl normalization is counted.",
    "literal empty regex wrapped in a noncapturing group; regression covers caller previous successful regex.",
    "record width fields retained in sort/group/resource scenarios; fixed-width masking preserves every matched digit position.",
    "derive client is flat compatible scalar/string settings; no false shallow-identity claim for general LMX copy/merge.",
    "copied Counter/Squares methods use actual copied lexical owner; Trace writes use explicitly qualified graph cells.",
    "regex comparison uses an explicit common byte/ASCII profile and declared shared matching engine; no claim to implement all Perl regex or every LMX Pattern facility.",
    "generic Perl bracket handles acquire/action/release failure and deterministic release failure precedence through eval; native defer is used only in client with infallible release."
  ],
  "async_contract": "All 24 scenarios are synchronous. State belongs to one Message; post the entire owner method for asynchronous execution. No cross-arena mutable pointer or extra scheduler, and posting action does not extend bracket resource lifetime.",
